# Known Issues & Tech Debt

> **Agent entry:** [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) · Canonical tracking: `docs/BACKLOG.md`. This rule summarizes the issues for quick agent context.

## Active Bugs (fix when touched)
1. **`startGame` race condition** — Uses `writeBatch` instead of `runTransaction`. A player joining during setup gets no target/task. Convert to transaction when modifying `startGame`.
2. **`endGame` doesn't clean up alive players** — Remaining ALIVE players keep that status when game completes. Set all non-winner alive players to ELIMINATED.
3. **Game code collision** — `generateGameCode()` never checks Firestore for duplicates. Add existence check + retry loop.

## Architectural Risks (be aware)
- **No server-side auth** — Any authenticated client can call `startGame`, `adminForceEliminate`, `endGame`. Host-only enforcement is UI-only. Don't rely on client-side checks for security.
- **Stale reads outside transactions** — `adminForceEliminate` and `recoverIdentity` read player data outside their transaction. The data could be stale by the time the transaction runs. Move reads inside transactions when refactoring.
- **`game.playerIds[]` drift** — This array is maintained separately from the `players` subcollection and can diverge. Prefer querying the subcollection as source of truth.
- **Weak Agent Key** — 3-digit PIN (1000 possibilities). Not secure against brute force. Acceptable for MVP party game.

## Tech Debt
- No path aliases (long `../../src/...` imports)
- No CI/CD pipeline
- No React component tests (only pure logic tested)
- Firestore rules exist but are permissive (any auth user can update any game/player)
- Firestore reads validated via Zod in `@/types/firestoreParse` (Phase 5)
